1105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 848 0 R
/T (Every story about power eventually has to answer the same question twice.)
/E (Every story about power eventually has to answer the same question twice.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 848 0 R
/E (The first time, it asks: what happens when one person has the power to decide for everyone else? That was Echo Protocol. That was Elias Voss, and the machine he inherited, and the choice Aiden Kade made to end a cycle that had already broken eleven other people before him. That was a story about a city, and a director, and a single unbearable night in which one man's certainty nearly cost three hundred and forty million people the right to remember their own lives.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 848 0 R
/T (PREFACE)
/E (PREFACE)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
