1114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 851 0 R
/E (It is also, if I am honest, a story about the particular loneliness of being trusted. Aiden spent Volume One learning that no one person should carry the whole weight of a choice like this alone.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 852 0 R
/T (Volume Two asks a harder version of that same lesson: what do you do when the whole weight of the choice comes looking for you again anyway, because you are, for reasons entirely outside your control, still the one person a much older and much larger power has decided to speak to?)
/E (Volume Two asks a harder version of that same lesson: what do you do when the whole weight of the choice comes looking for you again anyway, because you are, for reasons entirely outside your control, still the one person a much older and much larger power has decided to speak to?)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
