/E ("Dr. Kade." An elderly man near the front, a retired dockworker who came to nearly every session and asked, without fail, the hardest question in the room. "Six years ago you told this city the truth cost you something. You still haven't told us what." Aiden had answered a version of that question perhaps forty times since the Spire opened its doors, and it had never once gotten easier to answer honestly. "It cost me a dream I used to have," he said. "About a bridge, and a girl standing on it. I don't have it anymore. Some days I miss it more than I expected to.")
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [0]
>>
