/T ("That wasn't in any survey," she said finally, her voice tight. "That field shouldn't exist. It's not on any chart, not from any probe, not from anything we've ever launched out this far." "Could it be new?" Devan asked. "Something that formed after the last survey pass?" "It could be," Kalinda said. "It could also be exactly the kind of thing something old and patient puts in the way of visitors it hasn't decided to let in yet." She looked back at Aiden, and for the first time since the launch, some of the fearlessness had gone out of her expression, replaced by something more honest. "I don't love that as a theory. I love it less than not knowing." Aiden didn't have an answer for her. He thought, privately, that she was probably right, and said nothing, because there was nothing useful to say to a fear that was almost certainly justified.)
