/T (In one bridge, the sky burned a color that had no name. In another, the city below was perfectly, eerily whole, every window lit, every street full, and utterly, absolutely silent, as though the entire population had simply stopped moving mid-motion and never started again. In every version, a girl stood at the center of the bridge. In every version, she was Aris, and she was not quite Aris, and the difference between those two things was the exact shape of what was keeping Aiden awake at three in the morning, ship-time, staring at a ceiling forty-one days from the nearest solid ground. "You've got the look," Kalinda said, finding him in the observation bay on day forty-two, both of them nursing coffee that had long since stopped tasting like coffee and started tasting like the recycled idea of it.)
