/Title (not as a plot device, but as a genuine question about what a civilization owes the ones that came before it, and the ones that will come after. Every one of those twelve worlds tried to answer the same crossroads with only two doors in front of them. Aiden's real accomplishment in this book isn't defeating anything. It's noticing there was a third door nobody had thought to build yet, and building it anyway, at the cost of something he couldn't get back.)
